L266 COMPLETE: 1/3 checks PASS.
READING: assembly bias narrows the Desmond gap for stellar-dominated galaxies (2.0x -> 1.3-1.55x, marginal), but for gas-dominated dwarfs the
gas-fraction scatter, which no halo property correlates with, leaves the emergent scatter 2.2-2.4x the observed unless the observed dwarf
scatter is itself larger (Lelli+16 report the gas-rich BTFR scatter is NOT larger).  This is the sharpest live tension for the emergent
reading and the sharpest live support for a universal scale: the gas-rich dwarfs are where the two readings differ, and the record's G114
(55 gas-dominated dwarfs, 0.150 dex rms about g^2 = a0 g_N, zero bias) is the number to beat with a full LCDM population model.
